       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Sertraline 400 mg daily is twice the FDA-labeled maximum of 200 mg/day for adults. Higher doses carry a greater risk of serotonin syndrome, QT prolongation, seizures, and GI or bleeding effects. They haven't been shown to work better.\n\nWhich of these did you intend?\n\n1. **A dose within range.** For example, 200 mg once daily (the maximum), or a lower dose if you're starting or titrating. Typical starting doses are 25\u201350 mg daily.\n2. **A deliberate dose above the labeled maximum.** If so, confirm that it's intentional. I can enter it with a note, such as \"Above max labeled dose, intentional per attending, with monitoring plan.\" Check whether your pharmacy needs an override or a documented rationale.\n3. **A typo.** For example, you may have meant 40 mg or 100 mg.\n\nTell me the dose and I'll enter it right away."
